  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Humanitarian and Protection Environment for Rohingya in Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of the International Organization for Migration (IOM)&apos;s wider regional response in addressing the needs of displaced Rohingya, and as part of a coordinated effort with the Government of Indonesia, international partners, and civil society, through this project, the Organization is providing emergency humanitarian assistance to the existing caseload and recent arrivals of Rohingya who has fled violence in Myanmar&apos;s Rakhine State and have disembarked in Indonesia, regardless of their gender and age background. The project is addressing the humanitarian needs of Rohingya refugees arriving in Indonesia by providing direct assistance and strengthening reception and protection systems. The project ensures that the humanitarian needs of Rohingya refugees are met with the provision of humanitarian assistance and sustained care. On the other hand, IOM is building on engagement with key local and national actors to strengthen the reception system and protection environment for Rohingya refugees in targeted locations in Indonesia. The project targets 180 Rohingya refugees for humanitarian assistance and sustained care; 500 refugees and host community members to benefit from risk communication and community engagement; and 40 public officials to benefit from risk communication and community engagement.</narrative>
  </description>
